RUNS      10, all 8

SUBJECT   an async task's implicit Thread suspends mid-callee with nothing runnable, holding the
          instance's exclusive_thread; a SYNC-typed call (the parent's f, called back by a nested child)
          enters anyway and resume-laters it (#978). Task.enter_implicit_thread consults exclusive_thread
          only for async-typed entries, so the reference admits the sync call.

BURROUGHS, when this reading was committed
  hangs: the implicit Thread's giveBack keeps the run slot (the chain's hold), so the sync call cannot
  enter; and nothing outside a handoff or the YIELD arm would drive the readied Thread if it could

