  taken      2026-10-13T06:34:08Z
  host       Darwin arm64
  wasmtime   wasmtime 49.0.2 (3c8a3e79a 2026-10-02)  (-W component-model-threading=y -W component-model-async=y, --invoke 'run()')
  wasm-tools wasm-tools 1.258.0
  source     sync-enters-past-suspended.wat -> sync-enters-past-suspended.wasm, hand-authored WAT

  A first draft had the child call f at once and wasmtime trapped "cannot resume thread which is not
  suspended": an async-lowered callee starts eagerly, so f ran before run had suspended. The child now
  YIELDs first. The fixture's ordering, not the engine's.
